{"answers":[{"answer":"Approve all 32 requirements as one run.","by":"Hamza (via web)","id":"Q-9","question":"Should the 32 requirements be approved as one run despite the estimate of about three runs’ worth of work, or should the one-run scope be reduced?"},{"answer":"Allow the administrator to reverse the claimed release and record the intervention, without automatically revoking the claimant’s temporary parking authorization.","by":"Hamza (via web)","id":"Q-10","question":"When a Parking Administrator reverses a claimed release, should the claimant’s temporary parking authorization for that date be revoked immediately, or should the reversal be recorded without revoking that authorization?"}],"asked":[{"category":"errors","id":"Q-11","impact":3,"impactReason":"This determines who may use the space and whether it can be allocated again that day.","options":["Keep the space allocated to the original claimant for that date; record the intervention and do not make the space available to the holder or another claimant.","Return the space to the holder, while leaving the original claimant’s authorization valid for that date.","Return the space to the holder only after the administrator explicitly revokes the original claimant’s authorization.","Make the space available for another claim while leaving the original claimant’s authorization valid for that date."],"reason":"This preserves the specified authorization and avoids allocating the same space to multiple users.","recommended":"Keep the space allocated to the original claimant for that date; record the intervention and do not make the space available to the holder or another claimant.","score":9,"spans":[],"text":"After a Parking Administrator intervenes to reverse a claimed release, what should happen to the space, given that the claimant’s temporary authorization is not automatically revoked?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"errors","id":"Q-12","impact":3,"impactReason":"Role provisioning determines who can access privileged functions and records.","options":["Keep role provisioning out of scope; assume staff role assignments are handled outside this system.","Allow an existing Parking Administrator to assign or remove the Parking Administrator and Security Guard roles in the application.","Define a separate controlled process for authorizing and provisioning these staff roles."],"reason":"The request specifies staff roles and their responsibilities, but does not ask for a role-provisioning process.","recommended":"Keep role provisioning out of scope; assume staff role assignments are handled outside this system.","score":9,"spans":[],"text":"Should this specification define how Parking Administrator and Security Guard role assignments are provisioned?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"errors","id":"Q-13","impact":3,"impactReason":"Vehicle status and ownership determine which plate receives parking authorization.","options":["Require selection of an active vehicle registered to the claimant; deactivated vehicles cannot be used for claims.","Allow selection of any vehicle registered to the claimant, including deactivated vehicles.","Allow a claimant or Parking Administrator to choose whether a deactivated vehicle can be used for a claim."],"reason":"This adds the active-status check to the vehicle-selection requirement while keeping claims tied to the claimant’s own registered vehicles.","recommended":"Require selection of an active vehicle registered to the claimant; deactivated vehicles cannot be used for claims.","score":9,"spans":[],"text":"For a temporary parking claim, must the selected vehicle be active, or may an employee select a registered vehicle that has been deactivated?","uncertainty":3}],"checks":{"critic":[{"finding":"Rubric 1: REQ-13 preserves the claimant’s authorization after reversing a claimed release but does not define whether the space remains allocated, returns to the holder, or becomes claimable again, leaving allocation semantics potentially inconsistent with REQ-16’s no-double-allocation rule.","reqId":"REQ-13","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"Rubric 2: REQ-33 and REQ-27 assume authenticated Parking Administrator and Security Guard roles but specify no role assignment or provisioning path, so the spec does not define how legitimate staff obtain these privileges or prevent unauthorized promotion.","reqId":"REQ-33","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"Rubric 2: REQ-18 requires a registered vehicle selection but never requires that the vehicle be active and owned by the claimant, allowing the claim API to authorize another employee’s plate or a deactivated vehicle unless an unstated check is added.","reqId":"REQ-18","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"Rubric 1: REQ-14 requires notifications for every eligible non-dedicated employee, while AC-14.1 only tests employees with push enabled and does not reconcile that narrower condition with the requirement or Q-1’s instruction to notify all eligible employees.","reqId":"REQ-14","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Rubric 3: REQ-23’s acceptance verifies only that a stickered vehicle produces a plate-entry row, but REQ-28 needs to determine entry for a particular date and REQ-23 does not require that row to expose a timestamp or event date.","reqId":"REQ-23","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"}],"lint":[{"blocking":true,"check":"L1 ids","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L2 req-ac","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L3 ears","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L4 vague","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L5 nfr","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":false,"check":"L6 scope","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L8 anchors","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":false,"check":"L9 size","details":"This spec has 32 requirements, about 3 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.","fails":["This spec has 32 requirements, about 3 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut."],"passed":false},{"blocking":true,"check":"L10 trace","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L11 observable","details":"ok","fails":[],"hint":"Each Then names what a test reads, using at least one of these words: response, status, returned, row, record, call, request, sent, email, message, error, event, field, value, count, list, file, screen, page, shown, displayed. \"Sign-in succeeds\" fails; \"The response status is 200\" passes.","passed":true},{"blocking":false,"check":"L12 literals","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true}],"roundTrip":{"droppedSpans":[],"inventedCapabilities":[]}},"problemOf":{"Q-11":[1],"Q-12":[2],"Q-13":[3]},"problems":[{"kind":"critic","reqId":"REQ-13","text":"Rubric 1: REQ-13 preserves the claimant’s authorization after reversing a claimed release but does not define whether the space remains allocated, returns to the holder, or becomes claimable again, leaving allocation semantics potentially inconsistent with REQ-16’s no-double-allocation rule."},{"kind":"critic","reqId":"REQ-33","text":"Rubric 2: REQ-33 and REQ-27 assume authenticated Parking Administrator and Security Guard roles but specify no role assignment or provisioning path, so the spec does not define how legitimate staff obtain these privileges or prevent unauthorized promotion."},{"kind":"critic","reqId":"REQ-18","text":"Rubric 2: REQ-18 requires a registered vehicle selection but never requires that the vehicle be active and owned by the claimant, allowing the claim API to authorize another employee’s plate or a deactivated vehicle unless an unstated check is added."}],"round":2,"settled":[{"decision":"Should the 32 requirements be approved as one run despite the estimate of about three runs’ worth of work, or should the one-run scope be reduced? → Approve all 32 requirements as one run.","how":"answered","kind":"lint","problem":"L9 size: This spec has 32 requirements, about 3 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.","ref":"Q-9"},{"decision":"When a Parking Administrator reverses a claimed release, should the claimant’s temporary parking authorization for that date be revoked immediately, or should the reversal be recorded without revoking that authorization? → Allow the administrator to reverse the claimed release and record the intervention, without automatically revoking the claimant’s temporary parking authorization.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"REQ-13 cites an undefined ASM-31 and adds immediate revocation of a claimant’s authorization, a material behavior not stated in the supplied accepted assumptions or Q-2’s direction to reverse the release.","ref":"Q-10"}],"spec":{"assumptions":["Use Google authentication for authorized Folio3 accounts as stated in I-1; the email/password-only default in ASM-1 conflicts with that explicit requirement and is not applied.","A missing corporate employee profile blocks dashboard access; a recoverable error allows retry or support contact (ASM-2, ASM-15).","For a returning employee whose vehicle profile is incomplete, show the dashboard prompt and block vehicle-dependent actions until a plate is registered, following ASM-16 rather than the conflicting routing default in ASM-3.","The 30-day scheduling horizon counts calendar dates in the office timezone; dates are eligible for parking operation only when present in the administrator-maintained operating-day calendar (ASM-10, ASM-17).","The office-local fixed Monday report time is configurable; exact stakeholder addresses and time are configured by a Parking Administrator (ASM-25, ASM-26).","The LPR and indicator are the designated entrance systems using their selected vendor-supported interfaces; their specific vendor protocols are not defined here (ASM-9, ASM-20, ASM-21)."],"nfrs":[],"outOfScope":["Full audit-trail history beyond the expressly recorded release, claim, intervention, verification, and utilization records (ASM-12, ASM-28).","Custom report builder beyond filtered lists and CSV export (ASM-11, ASM-25).","Application and notification languages other than English (ASM-13, ASM-29)."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Google authentication callback identifies an account whose verified corporate email matches an active employee record in the corporate directory","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned session identifies that employee","when":"The callback is submitted to the sign-in endpoint"},{"given":"A Google authentication callback identifies a personal Gmail account, an account from another provider, or an account with no matching active corporate directory employee record","id":"AC-1.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401 and no employee session record exists","when":"The callback is submitted to the sign-in endpoint"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking system shall grant an employee session only when Google authentication succeeds for an account whose verified corporate email matches an active employee record in the corporate directory.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The corporate directory or current parking records contain updated values for an employee","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"The employee profile row contains the refreshed values from those records","when":"The employee signs in or an administrator saves the source-record update"}],"ears":"When an employee signs in or an administrator updates employee or parking source records, the Folio3 parking system shall refresh the employee profile and current parking assignment from the corporate directory and current parking records.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Google authentication succeeds but the corporate employee profile is missing or unavailable","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains a profile-retrieval error, no dashboard data is returned, and the error field includes retry or support-contact guidance","when":"The employee requests the dashboard"}],"ears":"If the corporate employee profile cannot be found or retrieved, then the Folio3 parking system shall deny dashboard access and return a recoverable profile-retrieval error with retry or support-contact guidance.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-2","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The directory and parking records contain a dedicated employee, an assigned floor, and registered vehicle details","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"The employee row contains the ID, name, dedicated-parking status, and floor, and each returned vehicle record contains its plate and stored make, model, and color values","when":"The employee profile is refreshed"}],"ears":"When a dedicated employee profile is refreshed, the Folio3 parking system shall populate the employee ID, employee name, dedicated-parking status, assigned floor, and registered vehicle records with license plate and any stored make, model, and color.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A non-dedicated employee has no registered vehicle record","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and the error field identifies that at least one license plate must be registered","when":"The employee submits a vehicle-dependent parking action"},{"given":"A non-dedicated first-time employee has no registered vehicle record","id":"AC-5.2","level":"manual","then":"The screen shown is the vehicle-registration screen and its form requires a license plate value","when":"The employee opens the first-login flow"}],"ears":"When a non-dedicated employee signs in for the first time without a registered vehicle, the Folio3 parking system shall require registration of at least one license plate before granting access to vehicle-dependent parking actions.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A returning employee has no registered license plate","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains dashboard data and a vehicle-registration prompt field","when":"The employee requests the dashboard"},{"given":"A returning employee has no registered license plate","id":"AC-6.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and the error field identifies the missing plate","when":"The employee submits a vehicle-dependent parking action"}],"ears":"When a returning employee has no complete vehicle profile, the Folio3 parking system shall show the dashboard with a vehicle-registration prompt and block vehicle-dependent parking actions until at least one license plate is registered.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-16"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An employee owns a vehicle record","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"The returned vehicle record reflects the requested change","when":"The employee adds, updates, or deactivates that record through the vehicle API"},{"given":"An employee attempts to change another employee's vehicle record","id":"AC-7.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and the other employee's vehicle row is unchanged","when":"The employee submits the change through the vehicle API"},{"given":"A Parking Administrator is authenticated","id":"AC-7.3","level":"api","then":"The returned vehicle record reflects the requested change","when":"The administrator adds, updates, or deactivates an employee vehicle record"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking system shall allow an employee to add, update, or deactivate only their own vehicle records and allow a Parking Administrator to manage employee vehicle records.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An employee has a dedicated assignment and the date is marked as an operating day","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"The response status field is Reserved and the assignment row identifies the employee","when":"The parking status for that date is queried and no release exists"},{"given":"An employee has a dedicated assignment and the date is not marked as an operating day","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"The response operating-day field is false","when":"The parking status for that date is queried"}],"ears":"While an assigned employee has dedicated parking on an operating day, the Folio3 parking system shall treat the assigned space as reserved for that employee unless a release is recorded for that date.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An employee has dedicated parking and has not released today's space","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned release record has today's date and Released status","when":"The employee submits one release action"},{"given":"A dedicated parking holder opens the home screen and today's space has not been released","id":"AC-10.2","level":"manual","then":"The screen displays a single action to release today's parking","when":"The home screen is displayed"},{"given":"A dedicated parking holder has released or has had today's space claimed","id":"AC-10.3","level":"manual","then":"The screen displays the current Reserved, Released, or Claimed status","when":"The holder views today's parking status"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking system shall let a dedicated parking holder release today's assigned space from the home screen with one release action and return the release status for that date.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A dedicated parking holder submits one or more operating dates within the next 30 calendar dates","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and a release row is returned for each selected date","when":"The schedule request is submitted"},{"given":"A dedicated parking holder submits a date beyond the next 30 calendar dates or a date not marked as an operating day","id":"AC-11.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and no release row is created","when":"The schedule request is submitted"},{"given":"A scheduled release date has arrived","id":"AC-11.3","level":"job","then":"The release row is marked available for claiming","when":"The configured daily release-time job runs in the office's local timezone"},{"given":"A holder schedules releases through the calendar","id":"AC-11.4","level":"manual","then":"The screen displays each selected date as scheduled","when":"The dates are saved"}],"ears":"When a dedicated parking holder schedules one or more future releases, the Folio3 parking system shall accept operating dates within the next 30 calendar dates in the office's local timezone and make each scheduled space claimable at the configured daily release time.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM-10","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A holder releases today's space before the configured daily release time","id":"AC-12.1","level":"job","then":"The release row is marked available for claiming","when":"The daily release-time job runs"},{"given":"A holder releases today's space at or after the configured daily release time","id":"AC-12.2","level":"api","then":"The returned release record is marked available for claiming","when":"The release request is accepted"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking system shall make today's release claimable at the configured release time when released earlier than that time, and immediately when released at or after that time.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","ASM-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A holder's release has not been claimed","id":"AC-13.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the release row has Cancelled status","when":"The holder cancels the release"},{"given":"A holder's release has already been claimed","id":"AC-13.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the error field identifies that administrator intervention is required","when":"The holder attempts to cancel it"},{"given":"A released space has been claimed and a Parking Administrator is authenticated","id":"AC-13.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, an intervention row identifies the administrator, affected release, action, and timestamp, and the claimant's returned authorization status remains authorized","when":"The administrator reverses the claimed release"},{"given":"A Parking Administrator has reversed a claimed release and the claimant's vehicle has no other authorization issue","id":"AC-13.4","level":"api","then":"The verification response is authorized and an indicator activation call is recorded","when":"The claimant's vehicle plate is submitted for entrance verification for that date"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking system shall allow a holder to cancel an unclaimed release and allow a Parking Administrator to reverse a claimed release, record the intervention, and do so without automatically revoking the claimant's temporary parking authorization.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","Q-2","Q-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A space becomes available and eligible non-dedicated employees have push notifications enabled","id":"AC-14.1","level":"api","then":"A call to the push-notification service is recorded for every eligible employee","when":"The availability event is processed"}],"ears":"When one or more spaces become available, the Folio3 parking system shall send a push notification to every eligible employee without dedicated parking.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A space is available and push delivery fails or is disabled for an eligible employee","id":"AC-15.1","level":"api","then":"The response includes that space in the available list and the available count is at least 1","when":"The employee requests available parking"}],"ears":"If push notification delivery fails or an eligible employee has notifications disabled, then the Folio3 parking system shall keep the available space claimable in the application.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Two eligible employees submit claims concurrently for the final available space","id":"AC-16.1","level":"api","then":"Exactly one response is successful, the other response contains a conflict error and refreshed availability, and only one claim row exists for the space","when":"Both claim requests are processed"},{"given":"An employee already has a temporary claim for a date","id":"AC-16.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the count of that employee's claim rows for the date remains 1","when":"The employee submits another claim for that date"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking system shall allocate each released space to the first successfully committed eligible claim, reject competing claims for an already allocated space, and allow at most one claim per employee per date.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-6","Q-4","ASM-18"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Released spaces have known available and claimed statuses","id":"AC-17.1","level":"api","then":"The response count equals the number of claimable spaces","when":"An eligible employee requests parking availability"},{"given":"An eligible employee opens the parking availability screen and available spaces exist","id":"AC-17.2","level":"manual","then":"The screen displays the current available-space count","when":"The availability screen is displayed"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking system shall return the current available-space count to employees without dedicated parking and display that count in the application.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An employee has multiple registered vehicles and an available space exists","id":"AC-18.1","level":"api","then":"The returned claim record contains the selected vehicle ID and only that vehicle's plate is present in the claim authorization record","when":"The employee claims a space and selects one vehicle"},{"given":"An employee has registered vehicles but submits a claim without selecting one","id":"AC-18.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 422 and no claim row is created","when":"The claim request is submitted"}],"ears":"When an employee claims a temporary space, the Folio3 parking system shall require selection of one registered vehicle and authorize only that vehicle's plate for the claim.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An employee has a successful temporary claim","id":"AC-19.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 or 409 and the claim row remains active","when":"The employee submits a cancellation or relinquishment request"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking system shall not allow an employee to cancel or relinquish a successful temporary parking claim.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An eligible employee successfully claims a space","id":"AC-20.1","level":"api","then":"The returned claim record contains the assigned parking floor","when":"The claim request is processed"},{"given":"An eligible employee successfully claims a space","id":"AC-20.2","level":"manual","then":"The screen shows the assigned floor","when":"The claim response is displayed"}],"ears":"When an eligible employee successfully claims a temporary space, the Folio3 parking system shall assign a parking floor and return that floor to the claimant.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Parking Administrator is authenticated","id":"AC-21.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the corresponding record contains the submitted value","when":"The administrator creates or updates an employee record, parking record, calendar, release time, report setting, or stakeholder address"},{"given":"An employee without the Parking Administrator role is authenticated","id":"AC-21.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and the configuration row is unchanged","when":"The employee submits an administrative configuration update"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking system shall allow Parking Administrators to manage employee and parking records, operating-day calendars, release-time settings, and report settings and stakeholder email addresses.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-2","ASM-17","ASM-25","ASM-26"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The entrance LPR system reports a pedestrian, motorcycle, or other non-car object","id":"AC-22.1","level":"api","then":"No authorization request is sent to the indicator system and no vehicle-verification row is created","when":"The detection event is processed"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking system shall ignore pedestrians, motorcycles, and other non-car objects reported by the entrance LPR system for vehicle authorization.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The entrance LPR system reports a vehicle identified as having a permanent Folio3 parking sticker","id":"AC-23.1","level":"api","then":"A plate-entry row is recorded and no temporary-authorization verification call is made","when":"The plate-entry event is processed"}],"ears":"When the entrance LPR system reports a vehicle with a permanent Folio3 parking sticker, the Folio3 parking system shall record its plate-entry event without requiring authorization verification.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A detected plate exactly matches a current-day authorization after case and permitted-spacing normalization","id":"AC-24.1","level":"api","then":"The verification response is authorized and a call activating the green indicator is recorded","when":"The entrance verification request is processed"},{"given":"A detected plate is partial, uncertain, unmatched, or has no current-day authorization","id":"AC-24.2","level":"api","then":"The verification response is unauthorized and no call activating the green indicator is recorded","when":"The entrance verification request is processed"}],"ears":"When the entrance LPR system reports a non-stickered vehicle, the Folio3 parking system shall normalize plate case and permitted spacing, require an exact match to a current-day temporary authorization, and activate the green indicator only for a match.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","ASM-7","ASM-9","ASM-19"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The entrance LPR system cannot read a plate","id":"AC-25.1","level":"api","then":"The verification response is unauthorized, the indicator remains off, and an attempt row contains an unreadable result and available timestamp","when":"The detection is processed"},{"given":"The camera, indicator, connection, or authorization service is unavailable","id":"AC-25.2","level":"api","then":"No green-indicator activation call is recorded and a security-alert call is recorded","when":"The entrance verification flow detects the failure"},{"given":"A service failure was detected while the authorization service was unavailable","id":"AC-25.3","level":"api","then":"A failure row with the available timestamp and failure result is returned by the attempt-record query","when":"The service is restored and failure records are flushed"}],"ears":"If a plate is unreadable or the camera, indicator, connection, or authorization service is unavailable, then the Folio3 parking system shall fail closed, keep the green indicator inactive, alert security for a service failure, and record the failure when service is restored.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","ASM-8","ASM-9","ASM-19","ASM-21"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A successful or unsuccessful verification attempt has been processed","id":"AC-26.1","level":"api","then":"The returned row contains a timestamp, plate when available, verification result, and entry-status field","when":"The attempt-record query is made"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking system shall record each entrance verification attempt with its timestamp, plate when available, verification result, and entry status.","id":"REQ-26","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-3","ASM-8","ASM-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A verification attempt has been recorded and an authenticated Security Guard opens the guard-facing view","id":"AC-27.1","level":"manual","then":"The screen displays the plate when available, verification result, and entry status","when":"The attempt is displayed"},{"given":"A Security Guard is authenticated and an attempt has no entry status","id":"AC-27.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the attempt row contains the submitted entry status","when":"The guard records whether the vehicle entered"},{"given":"An authenticated user is not assigned the Security Guard role","id":"AC-27.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and the attempt row is unchanged","when":"The user requests verification results or submits an entry-status update"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking system shall permit only authenticated users assigned the Security Guard role to view verification results and record vehicle entry status.","id":"REQ-27","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A dedicated holder did not release the space and no registered vehicle entry exists for the date","id":"AC-28.1","level":"job","then":"An unused-dedicated utilization row is created with the employee, vehicle, and date","when":"The utilization job processes that date"},{"given":"A temporary claim exists and the claimant's registered vehicle has no entry event for the date","id":"AC-28.2","level":"job","then":"An unused-temporary utilization row is created with the employee, vehicle, and date","when":"The utilization job processes that date"}],"ears":"When a reporting period closes, the Folio3 parking system shall record unused dedicated parking when the holder did not release or use the space and record unused temporary parking when the claimant's registered vehicle did not enter.","id":"REQ-28","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A reporting period has known total available capacity, occupied spaces, releases, claims, and released-but-unclaimed spaces","id":"AC-29.1","level":"api","then":"The returned value equals occupied spaces divided by total available spaces, released and claimed counts are separate fields, and released-but-unclaimed spaces are not included in the occupied count","when":"The utilization report is requested"},{"given":"Daily and weekly parking records exist","id":"AC-29.2","level":"api","then":"The response contains daily and weekly utilization values and the total available-space denominator","when":"An administrator requests the utilization report"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking system shall calculate utilization for each reporting period as occupied spaces divided by total available spaces, report released and claimed totals separately, and exclude released-but-unclaimed spaces from occupied counts.","id":"REQ-29","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-5","ASM-27"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The Monday report time is configured and stakeholder email addresses exist","id":"AC-30.1","level":"job","then":"An email call is recorded for each configured stakeholder address and the sent report contains unused-parking records, daily and weekly utilization, released totals, temporary-claim totals, and utilization percentage","when":"The weekly-report job runs at that time in the office's local timezone"}],"ears":"When the configured Monday report time arrives in the Folio3 office's local timezone, the Folio3 parking system shall generate and email the weekly utilization report to the configured stakeholder addresses.","id":"REQ-30","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-25","ASM-26"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Parking utilization records exist","id":"AC-31.1","level":"manual","then":"The screen displays the filtered list and a CSV file containing the filtered records is downloaded","when":"A Parking Administrator applies a report filter and exports the result"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking system shall provide Parking Administrators on-screen parking reports with filters and CSV export.","id":"REQ-31","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-11","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A utilization record identifies unused dedicated or temporary parking","id":"AC-32.1","level":"job","then":"No warning, suspension, or penalty event or record is created","when":"The utilization job processes the record"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking system shall not apply automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties based on utilization records.","id":"REQ-32","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authenticated user does not have the Parking Administrator role","id":"AC-33.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and the targeted record is unchanged","when":"The user requests an administrative employee, parking, configuration, or report-management action"},{"given":"An authenticated Parking Administrator opens the administration area","id":"AC-33.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned list or record is available","when":"The administrator requests employee, parking, configuration, or report management"}],"ears":"The Folio3 parking system shall restrict employee, parking, configuration, and report-management actions to authenticated Parking Administrators.","id":"REQ-33","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-2"]}]}}